<BaseLayout title="About | Shubham Gade" description="About Shubham Gade, Agricultural Engineer and PhD Researcher at the Asian Institute of Technology.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h1>From water management to precision agriculture.</h1><p class="lead">I am Shubham Gade, an Agricultural Engineer and PhD Researcher at the Asian Institute of Technology (AIT), Thailand.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section compact"><div class="container about-intro">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>My research focuses on precision agriculture, with particular interests in precision irrigation, crop water and nutrient management, remote sensing, UAV-based sensing, crop phenotyping, geospatial analytics and data-driven approaches for agricultural decision-making.</p>
      <p>My doctoral work brings these areas together through irrigation management, biochar, nitrogen variability, RGB and thermal imaging, multispectral sensing and machine-learning approaches for improving crop productivity and resource-use efficiency.</p>
      <p>Before beginning my PhD, I worked as a Young Professional-II at ICAR–National Institute of Abiotic Stress Management (ICAR-NIASM), India, contributing to geospatial research, agricultural information systems and remote-sensing applications.</p>
      <p>Alongside my doctoral research, I serve as a Teaching and Research Assistant at AIT, supporting practical teaching in Remote Sensing and GIS applications in agriculture and contributing to graduate research and publication activities.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="about-photo"><img src="/images/lab-research.webp" alt="Shubham Gade conducting laboratory research" /><figcaption>Experimental measurement and laboratory research.</figcaption></figure>
  </div></section>

